  var PLANET_HISTORY={mercury:'Formed ~4.5 Bya close to Sun. Giant impact likely stripped most mantle, leaving oversized iron core. Heavy bombardment cratered surface ~3.8 Bya. Cooling core created massive fault scarps.',venus:'Formed ~4.5 Bya similar to Earth. May have had oceans for billions of years. Runaway greenhouse boiled away water. Surface catastrophically resurfaced ~500 Mya.',mars:'Formed ~4.5 Bya. Had thick atmosphere, magnetic field, liquid water for ~1 billion years. Lost magnetic field as core solidified \u2192 solar wind stripped atmosphere. Water dried up ~3 Bya.',jupiter:'First planet to form. Rocky/icy core grew to ~10 Earth masses, swept up massive H/He envelope. Gravity shaped entire solar system \u2014 created asteroid belt, possibly delivered water to Earth.',saturn:'Formed shortly after Jupiter. Rocky core attracted H/He envelope. Rings may be only ~100-400 million years old (from destroyed moon). Cassini data: rings will vanish in ~300 Myr.',uranus:'Formed ~4.5 Bya in outer nebula. Earth-sized collision knocked it on its side (98\u00b0 tilt). May have migrated outward. Only visited by Voyager 2 (1986).',neptune:'Formed ~4.5 Bya, likely closer to Sun, migrated outward. Sculpted Kuiper Belt. May have triggered Late Heavy Bombardment. Captured Triton, destroying original moon system.',moon:'Formed ~4.5 Bya: Mars-sized "Theia" struck Earth. Debris coalesced in ~100 years. Initially at 14,000 mi (now 239,000). Magma ocean \u2192 anorthosite crust. Volcanic lava flooded mare basins.'};

