      diameter:86881, distSun:5.20, yearLen:'11.9yr', dayLen:'9h 56m', moons:97, gravity:'24.8 m/s² (253% Earth)',
      type:'Gas giant', maxMag:-2.9, angSizeRange:'30-50"',
      telescope:'THE planet for telescopes. Cloud bands visible in 3"+. Great Red Spot transits (use timing tables). 4 Galilean moons change position nightly — eclipses, transits, shadow transits. Always something new.',
      facts:['Jupiter\'s lightning is 1,000× more powerful than Earth\'s — and occurs in ammonia-water clouds where "mushballs" of ammonia-ice slush fall like giant hailstones','The Great Red Spot is a storm bigger than Earth that has raged for 350+ years with 400 mph winds — but it\'s shrinking and may vanish within decades','Jupiter\'s radiation belts are so intense they would deliver a lethal dose to an unshielded human in minutes — enough to fry spacecraft electronics','Deep inside Jupiter, pressure is so extreme that hydrogen becomes a shiny liquid metal — this exotic state barely exists anywhere else in the universe','Jupiter\'s aurora is permanent, 1,000× more powerful than Earth\'s, and is driven by volcanic material from Io, not solar wind','If Jupiter had been ~80× more massive, it would have ignited as a star — our solar system nearly had two suns','A 150-lb person would weigh 380 lbs on Jupiter — but there\'s no surface to stand on. You\'d sink through increasingly dense gas forever','Jupiter\'s magnetosphere is the largest structure in the solar system — if visible to the naked eye, it would appear 5× larger than the full Moon from Earth','Io, Jupiter\'s volcanic moon, is the most geologically active body in the solar system — 400+ active volcanoes erupting sulfur plumes 300 miles high, resurfacing the entire moon every million years'],
