    saturn: {
      name:'Saturn', symbol:'♄', color:'#e8d098',
      diameter:72367, distSun:9.54, yearLen:'29.5yr', dayLen:'10h 42m', moons:274, gravity:'107% of Earth — barely heavier than home',
      type:'Gas giant', maxMag:-0.5, angSizeRange:'15-21"',
      telescope:'Most beautiful object in any telescope. Rings visible in 2" scope at 25×. Cassini Division (dark gap in rings) visible in 4"+. Titan appears as a star-like point. Ring tilt varies from edge-on (2025) to 27°.',
      facts:['It literally rains diamonds on Saturn — ~1,000 tons per year. Methane is crushed into carbon by atmospheric pressure, crystallizing into diamonds that fall toward the core','Saturn\'s hexagonal north polar storm is 20,000 miles across — each side is longer than Earth\'s diameter. No other known weather pattern in the universe is hexagonal','The rings are 282,000 km across but only ~10 meters thick — proportionally thinner than a razor blade. If the rings were a football field wide, they\'d be 10,000× thinner than a human hair','Every ~30 years, a "Great White Spot" mega-storm erupts — larger than Earth, with lightning 10,000× stronger than terrestrial storms. The last was in 2010','Helium literally rains inside Saturn — helium separates from hydrogen and falls like rain, releasing enough heat to keep the planet warmer than it should be','Saturn\'s moon Titan has methane rainstorms, methane rivers, and methane lakes — a complete alien water cycle but with hydrocarbons at -290°F','Wind speeds at Saturn\'s equator reach 1,100 mph — nearly 5× the strongest hurricane on Earth','Saturn\'s rings may be only 100-400 million years old — dinosaurs may have looked up at a ringless Saturn. They could vanish entirely within 300 million years','Enceladus shoots geysers of salty water ice into space from a subsurface ocean — the water contains organic molecules and hydrothermal vent chemistry. It may be the best place to find alien life in our solar system'],
      missions:'Cassini-Huygens (1997-2017, 13 years at Saturn). Dragonfly (NASA, launching 2028 to fly a drone on Titan). No current orbiter.',
      tip:'Rings currently near edge-on (2025 crossing). Will reopen 2026+. Saturn\'s ring tilt is the #1 factor in visual impact.'
    },
    uranus: {
      name:'Uranus', symbol:'⛢', color:'#a0d8d8',
      diameter:31518, distSun:19.2, yearLen:'84yr', dayLen:'17h 14m', moons:29, gravity:'89% of Earth — slightly lighter than home',
      type:'Ice giant', maxMag:+5.6, angSizeRange:'3.3-4.1"',
      telescope:'Small blue-green disk visible in 6"+ at 150×+. No surface detail. But you can say you saw a planet discovered in 1781! Interesting challenge target.',
      facts:['Uranus was knocked completely sideways by an Earth-sized impact — it rolls around the Sun on its side at 98°. This means its poles take turns pointing directly at the Sun for 42 years each','Deep inside, water exists in an exotic "superionic" state — oxygen atoms freeze into a crystal lattice while hydrogen flows through it like a liquid. This state doesn\'t exist naturally on Earth','Despite being an ice giant, Uranus radiates almost NO internal heat — it\'s the only giant planet that doesn\'t. Something catastrophic may have "reset" its thermal budget billions of years ago','The magnetic field is bizarre: tilted 59° from the rotation axis and offset 1/3 from the planet\'s center. It doesn\'t even pass through the core — it\'s generated in the superionic ice mantle','Uranus has the coldest atmosphere in the solar system at -357°F — colder than Neptune despite being a billion miles closer to the Sun','Wind speeds can reach 560 mph but the planet looks almost featureless — extreme weather hidden beneath a deceptively calm blue-green haze','Diamond rain likely falls through the ice mantle as methane is crushed and carbon crystallizes under millions of atmospheres of pressure','Uranus smells terrible — its atmosphere contains hydrogen sulfide (rotten egg gas). If you could somehow breathe there, the stench would hit you before the -357°F temperature killed you','Uranus and Neptune are so similar in size that they\'re essentially twins — yet Uranus has almost no internal heat while Neptune radiates 2.6× what it receives. Nobody knows why'],
      missions:'Only Voyager 2 (1986 flyby). Uranus Orbiter & Probe is the highest-priority flagship mission per 2023 Planetary Decadal Survey. Launch possible ~2032.',
      tip:'Barely naked-eye from dark sites (mag 5.6). Use star chart to distinguish from field stars. Opposition: Nov 2026.'
    },
